7. Controller Documentation Strategy

We deliberately kept Swagger documentation lightweight. We added @Tag and @Operation to improve readability in Swagger UI, but did not fill every controller method with repeated response-code annotations.

Runtime HTTP behavior continues to be controlled by Spring controllers and GlobalExceptionHandler.

Swagger annotations document the API; they do not create HTTP status behavior.

This avoids duplicating centralized error-handling knowledge in every controller.

The approach keeps production controllers readable while still providing useful API documentation.

