11. Important Learning: Runtime vs Documentation

Springdoc can infer controller paths, DTO schemas, request bodies, validation constraints, and many success-response structures. However, it cannot always infer every downstream business exception or centralized @RestControllerAdvice mapping. For example, the application may return 404 through CustomerNotFoundException and GlobalExceptionHandler even when that behavior is not obvious from the controller method alone.

We therefore treat OpenAPI as documentation of the runtime contract, not as the mechanism that implements the contract.

