15. Interview Explanation

I integrated springdoc-openapi into both microservices to generate OpenAPI specifications and Swagger UI automatically from the Spring MVC controllers and DTOs. I added service-level OpenAPI metadata and lightweight @Tag and @Operation annotations so the documentation is easy to navigate without cluttering the controllers. The runtime status handling remains in the controllers and centralized @RestControllerAdvice; Swagger is used to describe and test the API contract, not to implement it.

16. Day 10 Result

Both Customer Service and Account Service now expose machine-readable OpenAPI specifications and interactive Swagger UI documentation, with professional service metadata and readable endpoint grouping. Existing tests and runtime behavior remain unchanged.